# The stem's files this node carries MODIFIED, each with the reason it differs.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR. `.offshoot-omissions` lists what this repo does not carry
# from its stem; this lists what it carries and changes. Everything else is the
# stem's byte for byte or this repo's own, so a diff against the stem reads as:
# the additions, the omissions (listed there) and these. A modified file is a
# conflict on every cascade that touches it, so each one here is a cost paid on
# purpose, and the reason says what it buys. A cascade reviewer meeting one of
# these files knows the node's side is a decision; meeting any other modified
# file, it is drift.
#
# AND IT IS CHECKED, by `scripts/check-divergences.mjs` (the tree's one copy,
# from template-svelte), run by `web/test/offshoot-divergences.test.ts` and by
# `scripts/apply-omissions.sh` during a merge: it fails on a modified file with
# no entry, on an entry whose file no longer differs, and on an entry with no
# reason. A file at the stem's OLD version is drift, not a divergence:
# `scripts/check-stem-drift.mjs` catches that.
#
# FORMAT. One file per line: its path, then its reason. `#` starts a comment.
# A line `[<branch>]` starts a section; this repo has one node, `main`, so it
# has none: every entry is what ronan-eth `main` modifies from
# template-svelte-tailwind-blog `main`. A child REPO never keeps these entries: its
# list is its own, written against this repo, and until it writes one it
# carries this file unchanged and the check says it has none.

# The workspace
.offshoot-omissions                              this site's own list: the template's two sample posts, which would publish as placeholder articles beside the real ones
package.json                                     the workspace's name, and pinnace, which builds the embedded projects
pnpm-lock.yaml                                   the lockfile with pinnace added
web/package.json                                 the build followed by `scripts/embed-projects.mjs`, which copies the embedded projects in
web/svelte.config.js                             the prerender crawl told that a project's `_site/` iframe is copied in after the build

# The site
web/src/app.html                                 the site's yellow loading accent
web/src/app.css                                  the site's dark base and yellow accent (and the comments' indentation, as prettier leaves it here)
web/src/web-config.json                          the site's name, description, URL, ENS name and colours
web/static/icon.png                              the site's icon
web/src/lib/components/NavigationProgress.svelte the bar's fallback colour, the site's yellow accent
web/src/lib/index.ts                             the path resolver's comments name this site's routes (portfolio, projects)
web/src/routes/+layout.svelte                    the site's footer and RSS call to action, dropped for the full-bleed project pages
web/src/routes/+page.svelte                      the home page
web/src/routes/blog/+page.svelte                 the blog index in the site's design
web/src/routes/blog/[slug]/+page.svelte          a post in the site's design (its title image, video and caption)
web/src/lib/blog/source.ts                       the posts' own frontmatter fields (title image, Medium link, video, caption)

